<main id="main" class="wide page-space"><div class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow muted-eyebrow">YOUR INFORMATION MATTERS</span><h1>Privacy & responsible use</h1><p>Plain-language information about this career-guidance application.</p></div><div class="panel prose narrow-panel"><h2>What we collect</h2><p>When you register, the system stores your name, email address, optional school and grade, and a securely hashed password. If you choose, it also stores your subjects, marks, ambitions, interest assessment and career recommendations.</p><h2>Why we use it</h2><p>We use this information to sign you in and help you explore careers that relate to your answers. Recommendations are generated using interest matching and academic information, not to make an automatic final decision about your future.</p><h2>AI assistant</h2><p>Chat questions and limited career profile context are sent to the application's recommendation service. External generative AI is disabled by default in this edition. An administrator must explicitly enable it; when enabled, questions and limited profile context may be sent to that provider. Avoid typing sensitive personal details into chat.</p><h2>Children and school use</h2><p>This application is designed for high school learners, who may be minors. Organisations deploying it must establish appropriate consent, safeguarding, retention, access and deletion procedures before inviting learners to use it.</p><h2>Current limitations</h2><p>Career reference data includes information derived from outside Lesotho. Some listed local programmes have not been independently verified. Always confirm admission requirements, course availability and financial aid directly with the relevant institution.</p><h2>Your data and support</h2><p>To request access to, correction of, or deletion of your account information, contact the school or organisation operating this deployment. The operator must publish its own contact details and full privacy policy before public launch.</p></div></main>
